# Body myths: true or myth?
subtitle: "Five things people say about your body, from cracked knuckles to swallowed spiders: true or myth? Guess each one, then hear the story behind it."

## Body myths: true or myth?
feedback:
    style: warm
    perfect: Your body has no secrets from you.
    good: A sharp eye for an old wives' tale.
    poor: These myths fool almost everyone.
    none: The myths won this round.
sources:
    - id: unger
      title: Does knuckle cracking lead to arthritis of the fingers?
      authors: D. L. Unger
      year: 1998
      finding: 'one man cracked the knuckles of his left hand, not his right, for over 60 years: no arthritis in either; Ig Nobel Prize in Medicine 2009'
    - id: hair
      title: The effect of shaving on the growth of hair
      authors: M. Trotter
      year: 1928
      finding: shaving did not change the colour, coarseness or rate of growth of hair
    - id: stomach
      title: 'Anatomy and Physiology: The Stomach'
      authors: OpenStax
      year: 2022
      finding: the stomach's surface epithelial cells are replaced every 3 to 5 days

    icon knk cites ["unger"] size 300 set twemoji x 500 y 450 icon_look picture of "hand with fingers splayed" hidden true
    text knk_l "Knuckles → arthritis" x 500 y 225 font_size 48 hidden true
    text knk_v "MYTH" #b5482e x 790 y 580 font_size 64 hidden true
    text rs_knk "MYTH" #b5482e x 140 y 310 font_size 36 hidden true
    icon r_knk size 165 set twemoji x 140 y 430 icon_look picture of "hand with fingers splayed" hidden true
    icon spd size 300 set twemoji x 500 y 450 icon_look picture of spider hidden true
    text spd_l "Swallowed spiders" x 500 y 225 font_size 48 hidden true
    text spd_v "MYTH" #b5482e x 790 y 580 font_size 64 hidden true
    text rs_spd "MYTH" #b5482e x 320 y 310 font_size 36 hidden true
    icon r_spd size 165 set twemoji x 320 y 430 icon_look picture of spider hidden true
    icon raz cites ["hair"] size 300 set twemoji x 500 y 450 icon_look picture of razor hidden true
    text raz_l "Shaved hair: thicker?" x 500 y 225 font_size 48 hidden true
    text raz_v "MYTH" #b5482e x 790 y 580 font_size 64 hidden true
    text rs_raz "MYTH" #b5482e x 500 y 310 font_size 36 hidden true
    icon r_raz size 165 set twemoji x 500 y 430 icon_look picture of razor hidden true
    icon ear size 300 set twemoji x 500 y 450 icon_look picture of ear hidden true
    text ear_l "More than five senses" x 500 y 225 font_size 48 hidden true
    text ear_v "TRUE" #2f6b8f x 790 y 580 font_size 64 hidden true
    text rs_ear "TRUE" #2f6b8f x 680 y 310 font_size 36 hidden true
    icon r_ear size 165 set twemoji x 680 y 430 icon_look picture of ear hidden true
    icon cal cites ["stomach"] size 300 set twemoji x 500 y 450 icon_look picture of "spiral calendar" hidden true
    text cal_l "New stomach lining" x 500 y 225 font_size 48 hidden true
    text cal_v "TRUE" #2f6b8f x 790 y 580 font_size 64 hidden true
    text rs_cal "TRUE" #2f6b8f x 860 y 310 font_size 36 hidden true
    icon r_cal size 165 set twemoji x 860 y 430 icon_look picture of "spiral calendar" hidden true

    card title "Body myths: true or myth?"

Your body, true or myth? First: cracking your knuckles gives you arthritis.
    draw knk knk_l

    quiz "Cracking your knuckles gives you arthritis. True or myth?"
        right: Myth. A doctor, Donald Unger, cracked the knuckles of one hand for sixty years and never the other: no arthritis in either, and an Ig Nobel Prize.
        * True
        + Myth

    draw knk_v

    pause 1.5

    hide knk knk_l knk_v

Next, the one that ruins bedtime: we all swallow spiders in our sleep.
    draw spd spd_l

    quiz "We swallow spiders in our sleep. True or myth?"
        right: Myth. No case has ever been recorded, and a big, breathing, rumbling sleeper is the last place a spider wants to go.
        * True
        + Myth

    draw spd_v

    pause 1.5

    hide spd spd_l spd_v

Then the razor: shaved hair grows back thicker.
    draw raz raz_l

    quiz "Shaved hair grows back thicker. True or myth?"
        right: Myth. The razor leaves a blunt tip that feels coarse, but a study in 1928 already found the hair grows back no thicker and no faster.
        * True
        + Myth

    draw raz_v

    pause 1.5

    hide raz raz_l raz_v

Now a school lesson: you have more than five senses.
    draw ear ear_l

    quiz "Humans have more than five senses. True or myth?"
        right: True. Balance, heat, pain, and knowing where your arms are with your eyes shut are senses too: scientists count far more than five.
        + True
        * Myth

    draw ear_v

    pause 1.5

    hide ear ear_l ear_v

And last: your stomach gets a new lining every few days.
    draw cal cal_l

    quiz "Your stomach lining renews itself every few days. True or myth?"
        right: True. The cells on the stomach's surface are replaced every three to five days, before its own acid can digest them.
        + True
        * Myth

    draw cal_v

    pause 1.5

    hide cal cal_l cal_v

You got {score} of {score_total}.
    draw r_knk rs_knk r_spd rs_spd r_raz rs_raz r_ear rs_ear r_cal rs_cal parallel true

The three family warnings were myths. The two from biology class were true.
    highlight r_ear r_cal effect circle
